Hi Guys, 
I've tried installing RH7.1 on the following system: 
* AlphaServer 2100 4/275 (1 x CPU) 
* 512MB RAM (1 x Memory Module) 
* ZLXp-E3 Video 
* 2 x RZ28M-VA disks. 
* Digital PS/2 Keyboard (from a Venturis 5100) 
* A4 Tech PS/2 Mouse 
CD boots fine (CD is fine. I've installed to an AlphaStation 255 from it)
but when it gets to starting kernel, it fails.
I've tried all the boot methods: 
>>> boot dka600 (my cdrom) [This starts graphical install I know, but it
freezes on starting kernel anyway] 
>>> boot dka600 -flags 3 
>>> boot dka600 -file kernels/vmlinux.gz -flags "root=/dev/scd0
initrd=images/ramdisk.img text" 
I must admit I haven't tried booting it with serial console. I didn't have
one hooked up 'til yesterday. 
I only want to run it in text mode for now, but I'm thinking that it's the
video card that is stopping the kernel from starting. 
I'm considering building a sable kernel on the AS255/233 and netbooting it,
when I find a power cord for the AS255 :) 
Has anyone got any ideas? 
Collin Baillie 
-- 
My other computer is a 4000 node Beowulf cluster. 

