Dear Ted,

I had problems similar to yours with my PWS500a.  I tried every combo of
boot flags and boot files known to man ...  the furthest I could get was
an aboot prompt from the Kickstart installation.

My machine also would not read from floppies.

the signature reply was

failed to open dva0.0.0.0.1

or

unable to find valid boot block (devicename)

or 

(device) has no media present or is disabled via the RUN/STOP switch

It was weird becuase the machine read the Compaq disks just fine.

Fortunately I had a semi-working Digital Unix installation on another
hard drive. Going into the DU equivalent of the /dev directory I was
able to see that the machine was unable to read some CDs, including the
RedHat disks, same with floppies.

Thinking it could be a MoBo chip going south,I ran the machine 24 hours
straight to warm things up.  That got me a working floppie.  Then I put
in an older, slower CDrom drive.  The new old drive read the RedHat
Cdrom quite well and my install went fine from floppies using the

boot dva0 -fl "" 

command 

It seems to me there is a lot of traffic on this list and to some extent
the Tru64 list regarding strange behavior by PWS AKA Miata-class
machines.

Your problems may possibly be to some degree hardware-related.

jn




