On Tue, Feb 19, 2002 at 09:55:10AM +0200, Ted Lufoma wrote:
> Hello
> Iam running Linux RH 6.2 and 7.1 on intel and sparc processors,
> and every time we have power failure for over 2 hours, which the UPS
> can sustain, i get a lot of 'manual fsck' on reboot,

Can't you just make your UPS to shutdown machines cleanly if a battery
is low?  NUT ( http://www.exploits.org/nut/ ) will do that with most
UPSes which are around and nut will recompile on Alpha.

You will need to do some adjustments in /etc/rc.d/init.d/halt script
but this is not a very big deal.  Also take care not to install
things you need on a partition which gets unmounted during a shutdown
before those things are used. :-)

  Michal




