"Ted Goodridge, Jr" wrote:
> 
> Has anyone gotten USB to work with alpha linux?
> 
> I'm trying to get an O-UHCI driver to work, it sees the hub and
> everything, but can't allocate the IRQ for any devices.
> 

I have a Belkin USB & Firewire combo card in my LX164.  It's a OPTI 82C861
chip.  I'm using kernel 2.4.17.  It uses the usb-uhci driver.
/proc/interrupts shows it on IRQ 26.  As far as I remember, the USB pretty
much straight out of the box.  The only thing I think I had to set up was
the hotplug and startup scripts.  I had to add a "insmod usbcore" to my
boot script before the mount of the fstab entries as usbdevfs needs the
core module.  The hotplug scripts handle the rest...

Alan




