"Rajiv Prasad" <rajiv.prasad@charter.net> writes:

> I am trying to install 7.1 on my 164SX, but am getting stuck booting
> into MILO.  I created the MILO disk using rawrite.exe as well as dd
> (under bash on UWIN running in AlphaNT on the 164SX), and I can boot
> into MILO fine using either floppy, but do not have any keyboard
> functionality at the MILO> prompt.

Unless you really need NT, you should install SRM instead of
AlphaBios, it boots faster and is better supported. If you can't, try
unplugging all serial devices (mouse, modem), MILO is sometimes
confused by them because it thinks they are a serial console.

        Falk




